    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Technical and extension support to 37 Palikas through LOA (37 palikas)

&#x2022;	Training to 345 Palika technicians, lead farmers, cooperative operators and farmers 

&#x2022;	5 Technical studies conducted

&#x2022;	2 Exposure visits for MoALD and NARC

&#x2022;	Exposure visits for Palika technicians, lead farmers and cooperatives (tentatively 112 pax)

Conduct final evaluation of project</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-	Provided continuous support and technical guidance to 37 Local Governments and cooperatives for effective implementation of planned activities

345 technicians, cooperative members, and farmers received training on production, plant clinics, soil and water 
management, postharvest loss management orientation, agricultural market management, farm record keeping


5 technical studies conducted; Financial incentive study, value chain study, GESI study, livelihood and returnee migrant assessment study, and packhouse study

-	Two Exposure visit conducted; 1) MOALD Secretary, VCDP Chair, NPD, NPM and focal persons of KOICA and UNDP paid a visit to Thailand and South Korea. It was to learn agricultural practices of neighboring countries and explore South South North cooperation opportunities; 2) 22 Agriculture Technicians (4 female, 7 from minority groups) visited India to gain understanding on India&#x2019;s extension system, postharvest technologies and cooperative management practices

112 Palika technicians, lead farmers and cooperative operators joined the exposure visits in domestic sites 

Conducted Final Evaluation of project</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
